## Real-World Example: Movie Databases

Streaming platforms such as Netflix and Tubi rely on large databases to organize and retrieve information about movies and TV shows.

A movie record might contain data such as:

```javascript
{
  title: 'Example Movie',
  genre: 'Drama',
  year: 2026,
  rating: 'PG-13',
  available: true
}
```

The database can support features such as:

- Searching for movies by title
- Filtering by genre
- Displaying movie details
- Tracking what content is currently available
- Organizing movies into categories
- Connecting users with watchlists and viewing history
- Helping recommendation systems find relevant content

The basic idea is similar to our smaller movie API:

```text
User → Application → API → Movie Database → Results
```

Netflix, Tubi, and other streaming services operate at a much larger scale, but the core concept of storing structured movie data and retrieving it through application services is similar to what we practice when building a CRUD API.

